# Gabay Project Rules

## Communication
- Always respond in English unless the user explicitly writes in Hebrew or asks for a Hebrew response.
- Keep explanations concise and professional.

## Architecture Quick Reference
- Backend flow: app/api/v1/ -> app/services/ -> app/models/db_models.py
- Frontend API: all calls go through frontend/src/api/client.ts only -- never fetch directly
- Response envelope: always { success, message, data }
- Hebrew dates: use app/core/hebrew_date.py (pyluach wrapper) -- never reimplement

## Development Standards
- UI components: use PageHeader and EmptyState from components/ui/ for every new page
- RTL: dir=rtl is set globally on <html> -- never override it
- Colors: use CSS vars var(--color-indigo), var(--color-gold), var(--color-bg) -- never hardcode hex values
- Soft deletes only: use the archived flag on Congregant -- never hard-delete
- State management: TanStack Query for all server state -- no Redux, Zustand, or Context for data fetching

## Backend
- Follow the layered FastAPI architecture and use SQLModel for database interactions.
- Use hebrew_date.py for all Hebrew calendar logic.
- Bulk operations use POST .../bulk-delete with a list of IDs.

## Do NOT
- Do not create global client-side state stores -- TanStack Query only
- Do not add new API route handlers without a matching service method in synagogue_service.py
- Do not use raw HTML elements (div, button, input) when a shared components/ui/ component exists
- Do not reimplement Hebrew calendar or date conversion logic
- Do not hard-delete congregants -- always archive
- Do not add obvious or narrating code comments
